  "details": "Not sure if this is a bug exaclty but wanted to record this behavior. \n\nAvatar chairs using an override controller such as the Splinks “fixed seat” animations, saw the following:\nSitting on an avatar chair caused the viewpoint to be correct but the avatar visible body was folded up and meters away. The Quest user changed avatars and back, then the chair caused the Quest user to stand on the avatar chair with the feet at the “hip” location (similar to what full body users do on PC). \n\nLoaded into a new world and the same result: first the chair caused the Quest avatar to be separated from the viewpoint, Quest user changing avatars then caused the standing animation.",
